EXT. FLOODED RICE PADDY - NIGHT

Moonlight on black water. A burned-out watchtower. Reeds rustle. Distant artillery thumps.

Four soldiers wade in a ragged line.

SERGEANT AUGUSTINE "GUS" ADEBAYO-KOWALCZYK, 40s, point man, signals with a fist. CORPORAL THEODORA "TEDDY" FAIRWEATHER-LINDQVIST, 20s, carries a radio on her back. PRIVATE MARCEL BELLINI-OKORO, 19, shivers, rifle held high. And MEDIC IGNATIUS "IGGY" NNAMDI-HART, 30s, limps, red cross faded on his sleeve.

They stop. Listen. The reeds sigh.

GUS
(whisper)
Hold.

TEDDY
Sarge?

GUS
Quiet.

MARCEL
I hear something.

IGGY
It's the water.

MARCEL
It's footsteps.

GUS
Both of you shut it.

A twig snaps ahead. All four freeze. A flare arcs overhead and bursts, white, turning the paddy to a lit stage. The soldiers dive into the water, sinking to their chests.

Silence. The flare drops. Darkness.

RADIO (V.O.)
(crackling)
Falcon Two, this is Base. Report.

Teddy grabs the handset, whispers back.

TEDDY
Base, we have contact. Grid four-seven.

RADIO (V.O.)
Say again.

TEDDY
Contact, four-seven! Repeat, contact!

A crack of gunfire. Muzzle flashes stitch the reeds. Marcel screams. Gus hurls himself on top of him, pushing him under the water as bullets zip past. Iggy crawls toward them, pulling a bandage from his pack. Teddy returns fire blindly.

GUS
Marcel! Marcel!

MARCEL
(spluttering)
I'm okay! I'm okay!

IGGY
You're hit.

MARCEL
Where?

IGGY
Shoulder.

GUS
Can he move?

IGGY
He'll have to.

RADIO (V.O.)
Falcon Two, hold your position. Air support inbound.

TEDDY
(shouting)
How long?

RADIO (V.O.)
Four minutes.

GUS
Four minutes. We can do four minutes.

Teddy and Gus exchange a look. Gus drags Marcel behind the burned tower. Iggy follows, hands slick. Teddy lays down fire in short, disciplined bursts.

IGGY
Hold him.

GUS
Got him.

Iggy tears the sleeve. Packs the wound. Marcel groans.

MARCEL
Sarge, I'm sorry.

GUS
For what?

MARCEL
I made noise.

GUS
We all make noise, son.

Gunfire slackens. Teddy ducks back, breathing hard.

TEDDY
They're pulling back.

GUS
Or flanking.

IGGY
Which?

GUS
Doesn't matter.

A drone in the sky, deep and growing. All four look up. Dark shapes sweep over the moon.

TEDDY
(whispering)
That's ours.

Fire blooms along the treeline. The earth shakes. The soldiers cling to each other behind the tower, water streaming from their faces, laughing and crying at once.

RADIO (V.O.)
Falcon Two, are you still with us?

Gus takes the handset from Teddy.

GUS
(into the radio)
Base, Falcon Two. All four. We're still here.
